  "tools": [
   {
    "name": "codex",
    "description": "Hand a task to OpenAI Codex, a separate coding agent on the user's own Codex subscription, and get its result back: use it like a subagent. It reads the whole project and runs commands; in write mode it edits files.\n\nCodex cannot see this conversation: write `task` as a complete, self-contained brief (goal, relevant files, constraints, what to report back).\n\nMemory: Codex keeps notes per project in .codex-bridge/ and reads them at the start of every run. For multi-step work give a short `thread` name: every call with that name continues the same Codex conversation. action \"threads\" lists a project's threads.\n\nPick `model` and `effort` per task (the model parameter lists the choices): luna at low effort for lookups and mechanical edits, sol at medium/high for ordinary coding, astra at high+ for hard design, deep debugging or a critical review; max/ultra only for the hardest problems. Defaults: the user's default, default effort.\n\nmode 'read-only' (default) reads and runs read-only commands; 'write' may edit files inside the working directory only: review its changes (git diff) before building on them.\n\nA run can take minutes. The result gives Codex's answer, the files it changed, the commands it ran, and how to continue."
   }
  ],
